### Test UpdateChildProfile Endpoint

@baseUrl = https://localhost:7089
@contentType = application/json

### 1. First create a profile to update
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChildProfile HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "nickname": "Test Child for Update",
  "ageInYears": 5,
  "ageInMonths": 3,
  "gender": 1,
  "supportNeedsLevel": 2,
  "mainDailyChallengesJson": "[\"Communication\"]",
  "strengthsAndInterests": "Loves music",
  "prefersVisualSchedules": true,
  "communicationMethodsJson": "[\"Visual aids\"]"
}

### 2. Get the profile to verify it exists
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChildProfile/GetProfile HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 3. Update the profile
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/ChildProfile/UpdateProfile HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "nickname": "Updated Test Child",
  "ageInYears": 6,
  "ageInMonths": 0,
  "gender": 1,
  "supportNeedsLevel": 3,
  "mainDailyChallengesJson": "[\"Communication\", \"Social interaction\"]",
  "strengthsAndInterests": "Loves music, animals, and swimming",
  "prefersVisualSchedules": true,
  "communicationMethodsJson": "[\"Visual aids\", \"Sign language\"]"
}

### 4. Get the profile again to verify the update
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChildProfile/GetProfile HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 5. Test update without creating profile first (should fail)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/ChildProfile/UpdateProfile HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer DIFFERENT_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "nickname": "Non-existent Update",
  "ageInYears": 4,
  "ageInMonths": 6,
  "gender": 2,
  "supportNeedsLevel": 1,
  "mainDailyChallengesJson": "[]",
  "strengthsAndInterests": "Test",
  "prefersVisualSchedules": false,
  "communicationMethodsJson": "[]"
}
